.TH T-CODE 1 "October 2026" "t-code 0.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
t-code \- lightweight C/C++ IDE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B t-code
[\fIOPTION\fR...] [\fIFOLDER\fR | \fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B t-code
is a GTK4 editor for C and C++ projects: a project file tree, editor tabs with clangd
(diagnostics, completion, go to definition, quick fixes), a terminal, a Search panel, Source
Control, git comparisons, Markdown previews, and building, running and debugging (with gdb) from
the editor. Other language servers (pylsp, gopls, rust-analyzer) are used when they are on
.BR PATH .
.PP
Given a folder, t-code opens it as the project. Given files, it opens them in tabs. Without
arguments it reopens the last project.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open an empty window that asks for a folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-send= "\(dqCOMMAND ARG\(dq"
Send a request to the t-code this runs in (from its terminal, a task or a plugin), through the
socket named by
.BR TCODE_SOCKET .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TCODE_SOCKET
The control socket of the t-code window, set in its terminals, tasks and plugins.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/t-code/
Settings (settings.ini), the session, snippets, styles and plugins.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/t-code/t-code.log
The last runs' starts, quits and warnings (Help: Open Log File).
.TP
.IR PROJECT /.t-code/tasks.json
The project's build, run, test and debug tasks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clangd (1),
.BR gdb (1),
.BR git (1)
.PP
https://github.com/suacayipkisi/t-code
